# A/B Testing & Conversion Funnel Analysis
### E-Commerce Checkout UI Experiment


## 📌 Project Overview

This project simulates a real-world **A/B test** on an e-commerce platform to evaluate whether a **new checkout UI** improves user conversion rates. Built entirely in Python, the analysis covers:

- Simulating a **5,200-user** experiment dataset from scratch using `NumPy`
- Running a **two-proportion z-test** using `SciPy` for statistical significance
- Building a **4-stage conversion funnel** → Visit → Add to Cart → Checkout → Purchase
- Performing **cohort analysis** by user acquisition week
- Generating **4 stakeholder-ready visualizations** using `Matplotlib` and `Seaborn`

---

## ❓ Business Problem

> *"Does the new checkout UI lead to more purchases — or is the difference just luck?"*

| Group | Experience |
|---|---|
| **Control (A)** | Existing checkout UI |
| **Treatment (B)** | New checkout UI |

---

## 🔬 Hypothesis

| | Statement |
|---|---|
| **H₀ (Null)** | New UI has NO effect on conversion rate |
| **H₁ (Alternative)** | New UI INCREASES conversion rate |
| **Significance Level** | α = 0.05 |

